# Backend declaration: claude (Anthropic claude CLI). The onboarding probe
# re-runs on any cmd.version change (declarations are promises, the probe
# makes them facts). Adding a CLI = a file like this; the ferry never reads
# backend names, only capabilities.
# TWIN DECLARATION: planning-workflow/runtime-scripts/backends/claude.kv is
# this same CLI's other declaration, under planning's one-shot launcher and
# its own key set. A claude CLI update moves BOTH; recalibrate the two
# together.
family=pty_tmux
cmd.launch=claude --model "{model}" --effort {effort} --permission-mode dontAsk --add-dir {workspace} --settings {profile} {bootstrap}
cmd.version=claude --version
prompt_style=positional
# SHARED PROFILE, BY CONSTRUCTION. profiles/settings-hooks.json holds no
# claude-specific content: it is the settings-JSON SHAPE, which any CLI
# wrapping Claude Code accepts, and its two workflow-owned hook commands
# (PreToolUse→heartbeat, Stop→record.sh stop-gate) are the WORKFLOW's harness contract, not a backend
# fact — codex.hooks.json carries them verbatim in its own shape. A third copy
# would be a third projection of one contract; 30-closure compares the copies
# that exist. Split this only when a real divergence appears, and let the
# divergence be the reason.
profile=profiles/settings-hooks.json
cap=pty,subagent,stop_gate,heartbeat,heartbeat_covers_subagents,warm_resume,nudge,takeover

# Frame-stability gap for the double capture (backends/pty_tmux.sh): the
# live-measured value for this TUI. Declared rather than assumed.
frame_settle=0.4
sig.working=(esc to interrupt|Thinking|Running command|✻)
# composer_line anchors the classification DOMAIN (last composer line -> end).
sig.composer_line=^[[:space:]\xC2\xA0]*❯
# NBSP tolerated on BOTH sides of the prompt char (prefix v1-measured, suffix
# live-measured; C-locale stripping cannot remove a trailing NBSP).
sig.awaiting_input=^[[:space:]\xC2\xA0]*❯[[:space:]\xC2\xA0]*$
sig.error_retryable=(API connection error|overloaded_error|Retrying in)
# Quota exhaustion is error_retryable's opposite: waiting does not help until a
# reset time the backend names. UNDECLARED IS NOT NEUTRAL — measured on a
# sibling declaration, where a quota-out pane read as idle and the ferry
# respawned into it (attempts born dead); for want of one line: the quota branch of
# pty_classify_screen is skipped, a quota-blocked pane classifies
# awaiting_input (the IDLE class, which the nudge injects into), and probe.sh
# falls back to the pattern `a^` — which never matches — so result=backend_quota
# is unreachable and a zero-quota window reports "onboarding probe FAILED —
# declarations are promises", blaming the declaration for a backend that is
# merely out.
# PROVENANCE, not overstated: this alternation is NOT live-measured. It is the
# superset of the wordings Anthropic's docs and issue tracker carry for this
# CLI (session / weekly / Opus limits; the "usage limit reached … your limit
# will reset at" form). validation-debt VD-25 closes it on the first real
# capture. The quota MECHANISM is already drilled (drill S9d, mock
# sig.quota_exhausted=MOCK_QUOTA); what is unobserved is this CLI's literal
# line. Note this is the OPPOSITE stance to codex.kv, deliberately: there the
# zero-state wording had no published candidates at all, so a pattern would
# have implied coverage the file did not have — here the candidates exist and
# the cost of waiting is a misclassification into the nudge path, not a no-op.
# The match runs over the VISIBLE pane (capture-pane without -S), and only
# inside the empty-composer idle branch, which is what bounds a false positive
# to one loud, relaunch-clearable park.
sig.quota_exhausted=(usage limit reached|hit your (session|weekly|Opus) limit|[Yy]our limit will reset at)

# 529 Overloaded — the backend is UP and refusing, which is neither idle nor
# retryable-in-progress and had no member of this vocabulary at all. LIVE
# MEASURED (one slice's postcheck round, this CLI at 2.1.259): 163 rendered instances of "API Error: 529 Overloaded.
# This is a server-side issue, usually temporary" over one pane log, 129
# unwrapped and 34 broken across lines — which is why the pattern is the short
# discriminator rather than the whole banner. Counted over the same whole log,
# sig.error_retryable's other two alternatives read ZERO: `overloaded_error` 0
# hits, `API connection error` 0 hits. So only `Retrying in` matched, and only
# while the ladder was still running; once it exhausted, the composer was empty
# and the pane classified awaiting_input — the ferry nudged a client that could
# not answer and failed the attempt as `idle`, twice, and then parked
# no_novelty on an identical fingerprint. Two attempts of the round's budget
# spent on a backend that was out.
# Same domain and the same bounded false-positive cost as sig.quota_exhausted
# above: matched over the VISIBLE pane only, and only inside the empty-composer
# idle branch — so a session that is working classifies `working` long before
# this is read, and the worst case is one loud park a relaunch clears.
sig.backend_overloaded=529 Overloaded

# The trust dialog's WORDING moved across CLI versions: the older build asks
# "Do you trust the files in this folder?", the newer one opens "Accessing
# workspace:" with a safety-check paragraph and a preselected "1. Yes, I
# trust this folder" choice — the old signature missed it and the dialog
# rode to unknown_screen (its choice line even matches the composer regex).
# Both wordings match on their distinctive trust sentence; Enter confirms
# the preselected choice in both. The workspaces/repos a session opens are
# workflow-provisioned (the topic's own checkouts), which is what licenses
# an auto-answer here at all; the recurrence cap (liveness.modal_acts_max)
# still bounds it. Recalibrate at the probe on any cmd.version change.
sig.modal.trust=(Do you trust the files in this folder\?|Yes, I trust this folder)
act.modal.trust=Enter

nudge_text=continue
